Dear Isabelle and Susan,

Could we meet online on Thursday 25 June at 10:00 BST to check the destinatio=
ns in the nine registers? I have attached the CSV of 117 original entry lines=
, with the register, folio and line retained, and a small working diagram for=
 Les Veill=C3=A9es du jeudi.

I would like to look at the =E2=80=9CB.=E2=80=9D on MRC/02 f.18r l.8 alongsid=
e entries where we can follow the wording as far as a recipient. The handover=
 from Valperche to Salle de Br=C3=A9vaux on the preceding line gives us one c=
omparison; the Rochemont receipt on MRC/03 f.9v l.3 is a separate entry, and =
I cannot yet connect it to the earlier one merely by the title and dates.

Isabelle, could you check the recipient column and notes against the copies, =
especially where the destination is abbreviated or the column is empty? Susan=
, could you see which destinations can be followed through the holdings catal=
ogue? For example, MRC/08 f.11r l.4 has a blank recipient field but names the=
 d=C3=A9p=C3=B4t de Valperche in its note. It would help to compare that with=
 what the catalogue can actually support, while keeping the original wording =
in the table.

The 117 are records, one per entry, rather than a count of people or routes. =
I have left the uncertain destinations open for us to examine together.

Many thanks,
Judith

